course: dictionary
lesson: 12868
title: Asking politely with enquire
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Enquire is a slightly formal way of saying ask. When you want information, you can enquire. «I will enquire about the train times at the station» means I will ask about the train times there.
explain: You will often see enquire on signs and in letters. «Please enquire at reception» means ask at the front desk. «Enquire within» means ask inside, or look inside for more information.
explain: Enquire can also show politeness. «The old lady enquired after his health» means she asked politely how he was feeling. The little word after matters: enquire after someone means ask how they are.
explain: Look at the words that follow enquire, because they change the meaning. Enquire about means ask for information. Enquire after means ask how someone is. Enquire into means investigate officially, to find out the facts about something.
fact: Enquire means to ask someone for information.
fact: Enquire can also be spelled inquire, and both spellings are correct.
fact: «Enquire into» means to investigate officially, to find out the facts.
fact: «Enquire after someone» means to ask how they are.
fact: Enquire is a little more formal than ask, so you often see it on signs, in letters and in polite stories.
exercise: «Please enquire at reception.» What does enquire mean here? | Sing a song loudly | * Ask at the desk for information | Leave the building at once | Write a long letter
exercise: Mia wrote, «I will enquire about the bus times.» What is Mia going to do? | * Ask about the bus times | Catch the bus home | Build a new bus | Ignore the timetable
exercise: «Enquire within» is written on a shop door. What does it tell you? | Buy something from outside | Keep out of the shop | * Ask inside for more information | The shop is closed for ever
test: «The old man enquired after his neighbour's health.» What does enquired after mean here? | * Asked how his neighbour was | Forgot his neighbour's name | Moved house with his neighbour | Shouted at his neighbour
test: Which word is closest in meaning to enquire? | Hide | Shout | Dance | * Ask
exam: «The council will enquire into why the bridge collapsed.» What does enquire into mean here? | Walk across the bridge quickly | * Investigate officially | Paint the bridge | Ask the bridge a question
